{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v1","paper":"erdos-68-factorial-denominator-irrationality","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-68-factorial-denominator-irrationality#res:divisor-channel-coordinates","an integer basis with prescribed weighted\nsums","<p><em> Set </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The vectors <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo></math></span> form an integral\nbasis. Every finite vector has the unique finite expansion </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>2</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-68-factorial-denominator-irrationality#res:finite-channel-moment-certificate","a finite formula for the gcd","<p><em>\nChoose a prime <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ℓ</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></math></span> and put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>H</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"]]}
